# miles-sandbox -- .gitignore
#
# Per CLAUDE.md "Repo layout":
#   results/ is the registry of every measurement (JSON + HLO text). Payloads
#   are NOT committed -- they are regenerable by re-running the tests, and
#   committing them would inflate the repo and create false provenance for
#   re-runs that overwrite. Reports under reports/ quote numbers and link
#   to the JSON path that produced them; the JSON itself lives only in the
#   running session, in Colab download artifacts, or in a separate archive.

# --- Test results: regenerable, not committed -----------------------------
# Keep the directory tree itself via results/.gitkeep so test code that
# expects results/ to exist does not need to mkdir defensively.
results/**
!results/.gitkeep

# --- Python ---------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Jupyter / Colab ------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Editor / OS ----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# --- Ad-hoc dumps and session artifacts -----------------------------------
*.log
scratch/
sessions/
.env
.envrc
